# Security headers for the canonical deployment at https://xnotary.digital
# (Cloudflare Pages). Vite copies public/ verbatim, so these land in dist/ and
# travel with `wrangler pages deploy app/dist` — the headers are part of the
# build rather than a setting someone has to remember on the hosting side.
#
# This reproduces exactly what production served on 2026-09-11; it is recorded
# here so a rebuild cannot silently ship without it. GitHub Pages ignores this
# file, which is fine: that origin only serves a redirect stub now.
#
# The site holds more than one app since 0.5.0, so this file sits at the root
# of the combined deployment (hub/public/ → dist/) with a rule per path.
# Cloudflare applies *every* rule that matches and merges their headers, so a
# per-path rule first detaches the general policy with `! Content-Security-Policy`
# and then states its own. Without that line both policies would be sent and
# the browser would enforce the intersection.
#
# The front page (/*) makes no network request at all, so its policy is the
# strictest: connect-src 'self'.
#
# For /xnotary/*, connect-src is the list that matters. It is the whole network
# surface of the app — three OpenTimestamps calendars and two block explorers — and nothing
# else. Adding a host here is adding a party the user has to trust, so don't,
# unless src/lib/ots.ts genuinely gained one. catallaxy is absent for the same
# reason it is absent from the calendar list: no CORS header.
#
# For /xsignature/*, connect-src is `'self' https:` — decided deliberately
# (decision D2 in the unification plan). xSignature's one network request is
# the opt-in RFC 3161 timestamp, and its "Another one" option lets the user
# type any timestamp authority's address, which no fixed list can name. That
# is broader than xNotary's list, and since the origin is shared it is broad
# for the whole origin's storage if xSignature's code were ever compromised;
# the feature was judged worth it. Its default authorities are listed in
# xsignature/app/hosts-in-build.txt. PDF.js runs in a worker loaded from this
# origin, and previews and downloads are blob: URLs.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' in style-src is load-bearing: Svelte emits style attributes
# (`style="margin:16px 0 0"`), and CSP counts those as inline styles. There is
# no matching allowance for script-src and there must not be.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

/xnotary/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://alice.btc.calendar.opentimestamps.org https://bob.btc.calendar.opentimestamps.org https://finney.calendar.eternitywall.com https://blockstream.info https://blockchain.info https://*.blockstream.info; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'

/xsignature/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https:; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
